--safe-mode (and --restricted, which turns it on) now keeps .yoyo/goal.md out of the system prompt and prints one line on stderr saying so. Committed as 9e6d85f9 with Fixes #1002. fmt, clippy with -D warnings, build and the full test suite all pass.

Before and after, using a test project whose .yoyo/goal.md holds a unique token, checked with --print-system-prompt:

| run | before | after |
|---|---|---|
| --safe-mode | 1 hit | 0, plus the stderr note |
| --restricted | not measured before the fix | 0, plus the stderr note |
| no flag | 1 | 1 (the goal section is unchanged byte for byte) |
| no goal file | — | no note, in either mode |

The note reads: ⚠ goal file .yoyo/goal.md not loaded into the prompt — --safe-mode skips project-authored text (/goal show still reads it). With plain output it uses no special symbols.

What changed:
• **Code:** a new `goal_block_for_prompt(restrictions, safe_mode)` in `src/commands_goal.rs` now builds the goal section of the prompt. `src/cli.rs` passes `safe_mode` to it instead of assembling the section inline.
• Tests:
  • With safe mode on, the goal section is dropped. A guard in the same test first confirms the file does load without safe mode, so the test can't pass on an empty fixture.
  • With safe mode off, the section is pinned with a full-string assert_eq!.
  • The note names both the file and the flag.
  • No goal file means no note.
• **Sabotage check:** I disabled the safe-mode branch with a `NEUTERED` marker and restored it in one command. Exactly `safe_mode_drops_the_goal_block` failed, by name; after the restore all 62 goal tests pass and no marker is left.
• Docs: `troubleshooting/common-issues.md and troubleshooting/safety.md now list the instruction files, memory.json and the goal file as skipped. Before writing that, I checked that memory.json and CLAUDE.md really give 0 hits under --safe-mode. My first memory test was invalid because I used the wrong JSON key (memories instead of entries`); with the correct key, the note shows up without the flag and is gone with it.

Left alone on purpose:
• `/goal check` is unchanged because it is already gated by project trust (#761). The commit says so.
• `/doctor` still lists fenced skill directories on the terminal. That output never goes to the model, so it isn't residue.
• The repository-structure map is still added to the prompt under --safe-mode. That is outside this task, and I didn't touch it.
• The `--safe-mode line in --help` doesn't mention the goal file. That line is broader wording I didn't change.
